ayed in the early years of the Irish Cup.","title":"Knock F.C."},{"sentence_id":5,"text":" Its ground was Bloomfield, which in 1882 hosted Ireland's first ever international football match.","title":"Knock F.C."},{"sentence_id":6,"text":" In 1882, the club changed its name to Down Athletics.","title":"Knock F.C."},{"sentence_id":7,"text":" By 1891 the club had ceased playing football.","title":"Knock F.C."},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Aldershot Football Club was an English Football League club, which was wound up in the High Court in March 1992.","title":"Aldershot F.C."},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" They became the first Football League club since Accrington Stanley to resign from the League during the course of a season.","title":"Aldershot F.C."},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" The club was nicknamed "The Shots" for both the last syllable of the town name and the military links to Aldershot.","title":"Aldershot F.C."},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" Aldershot were also the first ever winners of a Football League play-off competition, when they beat Wolverhampton Wanderers in the Division Four play-offs in 1987.","title":"Aldershot F.C."}],"peer_messages":["Unverified peer answer: FAI Junior Cup
